> **Independent Community Resource & Disclaimer**  
> This publication is an independent educational guidebook created by **SEDS Sri Lanka** to assist students and creators in participating in the hackathon. SEDS Sri Lanka is an independent non-profit student space organization and is **not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) or the NASA International Space Apps Challenge**. All NASA trademarks and event names belong to their respective owners.

---

### Empowering Sri Lankan Innovators for NASA Space Apps 2026

There is a special kind of magic in hackathon weekends. It starts with an open prompt, a few curious minds gathered around a screen, and the realization that NASA’s satellite observations, planetary missions, and climate records are free for anyone in the world to explore.

For seven consecutive years (2019 through 2025), **SEDS Sri Lanka** had the privilege of organizing and growing the **NASA International Space Apps Challenge** across the island, inspiring thousands of students to tackle global challenges using NASA's open datasets.

> *"The true flame of an expedition does not belong to the one who carries the lantern, but to every explorer who steps forward into the night. While we are not coordinating the stages this season, the legacy of ambition, grit, and late-night breakthroughs lives in every team across Sri Lanka. Keep building, keep competing, and let us see our nation shine once again on the global podium."*  
> — **SEDS Sri Lanka Legacy Note**

Our mission has always been—and will always remain—supporting the student community and elevating Sri Lanka's presence in space technology and STEM education.

---

### Exploring Your 2026 Participation Tracks

Whether you are participating through an in-person track or collaborating virtually, this open guidebook provides the essential links, timeline dates, and best practices to help you succeed in the **2026 edition**.

#### 1. The NASA Space Apps Universal Event (Global Virtual Track)
The **Universal Event** is the official virtual global location managed directly by the NASA Space Apps Global Organizing Team.

- **Universal Event Portal**: [https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/universal-event/](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/universal-event/)
- **Official 2026 Challenges**: [https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/challenges/](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/challenges/)
- **Find or Browse Teams**: [https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/find-a-team/](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/find-a-team/)
- **Who it is for**: Students and creators working remotely, teams with members across different universities, and independent innovators.

#### 2. Local In-Person Events
If you wish to participate in an in-person or community-hosted local event, explore the official directory:
- **Browse All Local Events**: [https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/)

---

### Official NASA Space Apps 2026 Timeline & Key Steps

1. **Step 01 — CREATE YOUR ACCOUNT (August 26, 2026)**:  
   Create a NASA Space Apps account or log in at [spaceappschallenge.org](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org).

2. **Step 02 — REGISTER FOR THE HACKATHON (August 26 – Nov 15, 2026)**:  
   Register for the 2026 edition on the platform to become eligible for Global Judging.

3. **Step 03 — CHOOSE AN EVENT (August 26 – Nov 15, 2026)**:  
   Choose an in-person local event or select the virtual **[Universal Event](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/universal-event/)**.

4. **Step 04 — JOIN OR FORM A TEAM (September 17 – Nov 15, 2026)**:  
   Assemble or join a team (up to 6 participants) on the **[Find a Team page](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/find-a-team/)**.

5. **Step 05 — SUBMIT A PROJECT (Nov 14 at 9:00 AM – Nov 15 at 11:59 PM Local Time)**:  
   Submit your project repository, description, dataset citations, and 240-second video demo on your team's Project Tab to receive a certificate of participation and qualify for Global Judging.

6. **Step 06 — COMPLETE PARTICIPANT SURVEY (December 1, 2026)**:  
   Provide feedback about your hackathon experience to help shape future editions.

---

### Looking for a Local Event?
If you wish to participate in an in-person or community-hosted local event, kindly check the official NASA Space Apps portal at [spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/](https://www.spaceappschallenge.org/2026/local-events/) and choose any listed events happening near you.

